1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:08,424
Sauti Pesa is a Swahili and English voice wallet for USDT. The AI runs on your own device, even with the internet off.

2
00:00:11,133 --> 00:00:17,181
First, the proof. This computer is online: a normal web request gets an answer.

3
00:00:17,531 --> 00:00:25,715
The app's AI and wallet run in a sandbox with no network at all: no DNS, no route, only the loopback interface.

4
00:00:26,065 --> 00:00:34,225
The engine checks this itself and refuses to start if the internet is reachable. Then QVAC loads Whisper and Qwen3 on the CPU.

5
00:00:36,933 --> 00:00:43,221
In the app, the status pill shows it live: AI on this device, network off, verified.

6
00:00:46,133 --> 00:00:51,293
A Swahili voice note: send my brother Juma fifteen USDT for school fees.

7
00:00:52,373 --> 00:00:56,861
Whisper transcribes it on the device, and Qwen3 turns it into a payment.

8
00:00:58,713 --> 00:01:04,641
Plain code then checks the contact, the address, the amount, the limits and scam signs.

9
00:01:04,991 --> 00:01:10,511
On confirm, the WDK wallet signs it offline, and it waits in the outbox.

10
00:01:11,400 --> 00:01:16,632
English works too. Here it is typed: forty USDT to Otieno for rent.

11
00:01:18,320 --> 00:01:22,928
The side panel shows what ran on this CPU, and how long each step took.

12
00:01:26,767 --> 00:01:33,271
Now an address-poisoning attack: an address that starts and ends like Amina's, but is not hers.

13
00:01:39,260 --> 00:01:43,100
The code blocks it, and a blocked payment cannot be confirmed.

14
00:01:47,033 --> 00:01:50,873
Check-a-message mode: paste a suspicious text message.

15
00:01:55,030 --> 00:02:01,390
A Swahili prize message that asks for a fee first is rated high risk, and the app says why.

16
00:02:08,210 --> 00:02:13,562
Above fifty USDT, the amount must be typed again before anything is signed.

17
00:02:18,567 --> 00:02:24,303
Back online, a separate sender with no keys broadcasts the signed payments, in nonce order.

18
00:02:34,865 --> 00:02:38,945
Each raw transaction is checked against its outbox record first.

19
00:02:40,700 --> 00:02:48,764
Here is one of them on the Sepolia explorer, opened once the explorer had indexed it: test USDT, signed offline on this machine.

20
00:02:50,767 --> 00:02:55,615
Sauti Pesa, by Swift Bot Labs. Own your AI, own your money.

